class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-badges _nghost-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----></ds-themed-status-badge><!----></ds-status-badge><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363=""><ds-type-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="pe-1" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-type-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="sr-only">Item type:</span><span class="badge bg-info">Ítem</span><span class="sr-only">, </span></span><!----></ds-themed-type-badge><!----></ds-type-badge><ds-access-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-access-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-themed-access-status-badge><!----></ds-access-status-badge><!----></div></ds-themed-badges><!----></ds-badges><!----></div><ds-truncatable _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c1371919000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1371919000=""><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="lead item-list-title dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/bf7056bb-1ae6-4aac-957d-fbf39499ba2b" target="_self">Exploring the neighborhood of thermotolerant free-living amoebae in Costa Rican natural water reservoirs as a preliminary One Health approach in the field</a><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="text-muted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-1 min-1"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"> (<!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-date ng-star-inserted">2026</span><!---->) <!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-authors ng-star-inserted"><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Alvarado Ocampo, Johan</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Castro Gutiérrez, Víctor</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Ruiz Campos, Marco</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Chaves Monge, Frida</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Silva Mena, Kevin</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></span><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-abstract ng-star-inserted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-3 min-3"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="">Free-living amoebae (FLA) of the Vahlkampfiidae family are widely distributed in nature, occupying aquatic and terrestrial habitats. The group includes thermophilic amphizoic organisms such as Naegleria fowleri. This study aims to describe natural recreational freshwaters in terms of the presence of thermotolerant vahlkampfiids, sediment microbial communities and climatic/land use features.  Water samples were collected from 24 locations from Costa Rica. DNA was extracted from FLA cultivated at 42 °C and molecular identification using family and N. fowleri species-specific primers for conventional PCR was performed. DNA extractions of sediment samples were also performed for a microbial metabarcoding characterization approach through 16S rRNA V3-V4 region and 18S rRNA V4 region gene amplicons sequencing. A geographic information system was used to locate each sampling site in its respective climatic subregion and to establish a land use coverage buffer around it. Results revealed 20 positive locations for vahlkampfiids; the sites predominantly featured forest cover and were in climatic subregions with significant rainfall patterns. All locations were negative for N. fowleri; however, identification by sequencing detected a predominance of Tetramitus spp., followed by Vahlkampfia sp. and Neovahlkampfia sp. Sediment metabarcoding showed mainly metazoans, microalgae and Proteobacteria in these benthic ecosystems. Even when N. fowleri was not found, our exploration showed that these aquatic environments of close human contact allow the presence of thermotolerant vahlkampfiids and might be surrounded by microbial communities of interest for future research regarding ecological interactions and public health risks.</span></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></div><!----></div></ds-truncatable><!----></div></div></ds-item-search-result-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></ds-item-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></li><li _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="my-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3 ng-star-inserted" style=""><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="pb-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-search-result-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="row"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-3 col-md-2 ng-star-inserted"><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" tabindex="-1" class="dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9" target="_self"><ds-thumbnail _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-thumbnail _nghost-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail limit-width"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content outer ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="inner"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="centered"><ds-loading _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-loading _nghost-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="spinner spinner-border ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="sr-only">Cargando...</span></div><!----></ds-themed-loading><!----></ds-loading></div></div></div><!----><img _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content img-fluid d-none ng-star-inserted" src="" alt="Miniatura"><!----><!----></div></ds-themed-thumbnail><!----></ds-thumbnail></a><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-9"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="d-flex"><ds-badges _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-badges _nghost-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----></ds-themed-status-badge><!----></ds-status-badge><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363=""><ds-type-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="pe-1" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-type-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="sr-only">Item type:</span><span class="badge bg-info">Ítem</span><span class="sr-only">, </span></span><!----></ds-themed-type-badge><!----></ds-type-badge><ds-access-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-access-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-themed-access-status-badge><!----></ds-access-status-badge><!----></div></ds-themed-badges><!----></ds-badges><!----></div><ds-truncatable _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c1371919000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1371919000=""><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="lead item-list-title dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9" target="_self">Dolarización financiera y rentabilidad bancaria en Costa Rica: un análisis empírico del impacto de la especialización en productos en dólares con enfoque econométrico y regulatorio</a><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="text-muted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-1 min-1"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"> (<!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-date ng-star-inserted">2026</span><!---->) <!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-authors ng-star-inserted"><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Abarca Chinchilla, Óscar Eduardo</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Astorga Hernández, Édgar Eduardo</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Castillo Castro, César Augusto</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Cantillo Simón, Miguel</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></span><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-abstract ng-star-inserted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-3 min-3"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="">Esta investigación analiza la relación entre el grado de especialización en productos financieros denominados en dólares y la rentabilidad de los bancos comerciales costarricenses entre enero del 2008 y diciembre del 2025. Combina un análisis descriptivo, la estimación de un panel dinámico de coeficientes heterogéneos con dependencia transversal mediante el enfoque Common Correlated Effects Mean Group (CCEMG) de Chudik y Pesaran (2015) —complementada con ejercicios de robustez de efectos fijos dinámicos y errores estándar de Driscoll y Kraay (1998)— y una discusión regulatoria comparada. Como variable dependiente se utiliza un ROE ajustado que aísla el efecto contable de la revaluación cambiaria. La evidencia descriptiva muestra una diferenciación estructural persistente entre bancos públicos y privados, con posiciones cambiarias y carteras en dólares mayores en estos últimos. Los resultados econométricos indican que la dolarización de la cartera no es un determinante significativo del ROE a nivel sistémico; la rentabilidad se explica consistentemente por la persistencia del ROE, la capitalización y la eficiencia operativa, destacando la diversificación de ingresos como el determinante de mayor impacto positivo. Además, un aumento de 1 p.p. en la tasa de depreciación mensual del colón reduce el ROE operativo en 0.18 p.p., aun tras aislar la revaluación contable. Así, el crédito en dólares opera más como instrumento de captación y fidelización de clientes que como fuente de rédito: la banca privada asume riesgos cambiarios y crediticios significativos sin una contraprestación clara en el retorno ajustado por riesgo. A la luz de la experiencia de Turquía, Uruguay y Ecuador, ello refuerza la necesidad de fortalecer el marco prudencial costarricense, en particular la prueba de tensión BUST aplicada por la SUGEF.</span></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></div><!----></div></ds-truncatable><!----></div></div></ds-item-search-result-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></ds-item-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></li><li _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="my-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3 ng-star-inserted" style=""><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="pb-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-search-result-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="row"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-3 col-md-2 ng-star-inserted"><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" tabindex="-1" class="dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df" target="_self"><ds-thumbnail _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-thumbnail _nghost-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail limit-width"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content outer ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="inner"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="centered"><ds-loading _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-loading _nghost-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="spinner spinner-border ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="sr-only">Cargando...</span></div><!----></ds-themed-loading><!----></ds-loading></div></div></div><!----><img _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content img-fluid d-none ng-star-inserted" src="" alt="Miniatura"><!----><!----></div></ds-themed-thumbnail><!----></ds-thumbnail></a><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-9"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="d-flex"><ds-badges _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-badges _nghost-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----></ds-themed-status-badge><!----></ds-status-badge><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363=""><ds-type-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="pe-1" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-type-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="sr-only">Item type:</span><span class="badge bg-info">Ítem</span><span class="sr-only">, </span></span><!----></ds-themed-type-badge><!----></ds-type-badge><ds-access-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-access-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-themed-access-status-badge><!----></ds-access-status-badge><!----></div></ds-themed-badges><!----></ds-badges><!----></div><ds-truncatable _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c1371919000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1371919000=""><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="lead item-list-title dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df" target="_self">La transgresión del límite (πεῖρας) como problema fundamental del filosofar en el poema de Parménides</a><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="text-muted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-1 min-1"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"> (<!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-date ng-star-inserted">2026</span><!---->) <!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-authors ng-star-inserted"><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Mata Quintero, Luis Enrique</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Fallas López, Luis Alberto</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></span><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-abstract ng-star-inserted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-3 min-3"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="">Esta investigación aborda el problema de la transgresión del límite (πεῖρας) como eje interpretativo de la filosofía de Parménides, proponiendo una lectura que integra los aspectos poéticos, religiosos y filosóficos del Poema. Frente a la tendencia de la tradición interpretativa a centrarse exclusivamente en la noción de límite, este estudio sostiene que el pensamiento parmenídeo no solo lo establece, sino que también piensa la posibilidad de su exceso, es decir, la inclinación del filosofar mismo a transgredir dichos límites. 

El trabajo parte de la hipótesis de que el filosofar en Parménides implica, de manera constitutiva, una condición transgresora del pensar, aunque la idea de transgresión no debe entenderse de manera unívoca, pues si bien el pensar tiende al exceso, no todo exceso es ilegítimo. La investigación distingue entre exceso —como impulso hacia lo desconocido y apertura del pensar— y transgresión —como quiebre ilegítimo de los límites de lo posible— , y muestra que la tensión entre ambos constituye el núcleo de la experiencia filosófica. 

Para fundamentar esta tesis, se examina el contexto pre-parmenídeo del problema, desde la épica de Homero y Hesíodo hasta los filósofos milesios, pitagóricos, Jenófanes y Heráclito, donde el límite se concibe como la distancia entre lo humano y lo divino. A partir de este trasfondo, en el segundo capítulo se ofrece una relectura del Proemio como una metáfora del ingreso a la filosofía, en la que el κοῦρος simboliza el tránsito del mortal hacia un ámbito reservado a los dioses. El viaje descrito por el Poema se interpreta como una experiencia limítrofe en la que el pensamiento, movido por el exceso, arriesga incurrir en la transgresión. En el tercer capítulo, el estudio se centra en la revelación de la Diosa, mostrando que el conocimiento verdadero posee un carácter excesivo para los mortales: el νοεῖν que capta el ἐόν trasciende la condición humana y exige una transformación del pensamiento. A través del análisis de los fragmentos B 1, 2, 3, 6 y 7, se concluye que Parménides no se limita a fijar los límites del pensar, sino que invita a explorarlos, asumiendo el riesgo inherente de la transgresión. 

De este modo, la tesis demuestra que la filosofía parmenídea surge de una tensión fundamental entre el límite y su transgresión, entre la necesidad de contener el pensar y la inclinación inevitable a desbordarlo. Pensar el límite implica, en Parménides, rozar lo inalcanzable, y es precisamente en ese gesto donde el filosofar se revela como una forma de exceso constitutivo del pensamiento mismo.</span></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></div><!----></div></ds-truncatable><!----></div></div></ds-item-search-result-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></ds-item-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></li><li _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="my-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3 ng-star-inserted" style=""><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="pb-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-search-result-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="row"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-3 col-md-2 ng-star-inserted"><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" tabindex="-1" class="dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/766d4068-f6de-4a41-a76d-a88fd2ede4d7" target="_self"><ds-thumbnail _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-thumbnail _nghost-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail limit-width"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content outer ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="inner"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="centered"><ds-loading _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-loading _nghost-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="spinner spinner-border ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="sr-only">Cargando...</span></div><!----></ds-themed-loading><!----></ds-loading></div></div></div><!----><img _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content img-fluid d-none ng-star-inserted" src="" alt="Miniatura"><!----><!----></div></ds-themed-thumbnail><!----></ds-thumbnail></a><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-9"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="d-flex"><ds-badges _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-badges _nghost-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----></ds-themed-status-badge><!----></ds-status-badge><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363=""><ds-type-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="pe-1" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-type-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="sr-only">Item type:</span><span class="badge bg-info">Ítem</span><span class="sr-only">, </span></span><!----></ds-themed-type-badge><!----></ds-type-badge><ds-access-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-access-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-themed-access-status-badge><!----></ds-access-status-badge><!----></div></ds-themed-badges><!----></ds-badges><!----></div><ds-truncatable _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c1371919000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1371919000=""><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="lead item-list-title dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/766d4068-f6de-4a41-a76d-a88fd2ede4d7" target="_self">Generación de una base hidrográfica ottocodificada y estimación de un potencial de crecidas a partir de índices geomorfométicos en el sistema de drenaje del río Damas. San José y Cartago, Costa Rica</a><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="text-muted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-1 min-1"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"> (<!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-date ng-star-inserted">2026</span><!---->) <!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-authors ng-star-inserted"><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Villavicencio Rojas, Herberth</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Quesada Román, Adolfo</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></span><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-abstract ng-star-inserted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-3 min-3"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="">La investigación tuvo como objetivo desarrollar una Base Hidrográfica Ottocodificada (BHO) para el sistema de drenaje del río Damas, ubicado en los cantones de Desamparados, La Unión y Curridabat, Costa Rica. El estudio surge ante la necesidad de contar con una cartografía hidrográfica oficial, precisa y jerarquizada que contribuya al ordenamiento territorial, la gestión integrada de los recursos hídricos y la reducción del riesgo de inundaciones. Actualmente, Costa Rica carece de una delimitación oficial de cuencas hidrográficas de alta resolución, lo que genera inconsistencias entre los distintos productos cartográficos utilizados por las instituciones públicas. Para atender esta problemática, se implementó el método de Otto Pfafstetter, una metodología de codificación hidrográfica reconocida internacionalmente por permitir la identificación única y jerárquica de las unidades de drenaje.

La unidad de análisis fue el sistema de drenaje del río Damas, de aproximadamente 25,8 km², caracterizado por una importante urbanización y una alta recurrencia de eventos de inundación. A partir de ortofotos y datos altimétricos oficiales se generó un Modelo Digital de Elevación de alta resolución, que permitió calcular direcciones y acumulaciones de flujo, delimitar las Áreas de Contribución Hidrográfica (ACH) e identificar los trechos de drenaje, elementos esenciales para construir una Base Hidrográfica Ottocodificada (BHO). La aplicación de la metodología de ottocodificación permitió establecer dos niveles de jerarquización hidrográfica, asignando códigos únicos a cada ACH y a cada trecho de drenaje, manteniendo una relación uno a uno entre ambos elementos. Además, se comprobó la posibilidad de integrar el sistema del río Damas dentro de sistemas hidrográficos mayores, garantizando la consistencia y escalabilidad de la codificación.

Paralelamente, se realizó una caracterización geomorfométrica de todas las unidades hidrográficas delimitadas. Se calcularon índices asociados a la forma de las cuencas, las características de la red de drenaje y las condiciones del relieve. Entre los principales indicadores utilizados se encuentran el índice de compacidad de Gravelius, el factor de forma de Horton, la razón de bifurcación, el tiempo de concentración, las pendientes medias, el Stream Power Index (SPI), el Topographic Wetness Index (TWI), así como los índices NDWI y MNDWI derivados de imágenes Sentinel 2.

Con base en estos indicadores se construyó una metodología multicriterio para clasificar cada ACH según su potencial de crecidas en categorías alta, media o baja. Los resultados evidenciaron que las zonas con mayor potencial de crecidas se concentran principalmente en las partes bajas y medias del sistema hidrográfico, coincidiendo con áreas urbanas densamente pobladas y con sectores históricamente afectados por inundaciones reportadas por la Comisión Nacional de Emergencias y la Municipalidad de Desamparados.

Se demostró que la combinación de una Base Hidrográfica Ottocodificada con indicadores geomorfométricos constituye una herramienta robusta para identificar áreas prioritarias de monitoreo, inversión e intervención en materia de gestión del riesgo. Asimismo, facilita la integración de información geoespacial procedente de diferentes instituciones mediante un sistema de referencia hidrográfico único.</span></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></div><!----></div></ds-truncatable><!----></div></div></ds-item-search-result-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></ds-item-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></li><li _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="my-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3 ng-star-inserted" style=""><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" class="pb-4 ng-tns-c1978743132-3" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-listable-object-component-loader _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3072932898="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3457600916=""><ds-item-search-result-list-element _nghost-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="row"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-3 col-md-2 ng-star-inserted"><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" tabindex="-1" class="dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/a0eca249-57ed-4111-931e-a3581259d4fb" target="_self"><ds-thumbnail _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-thumbnail _nghost-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail limit-width"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content outer ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="inner"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="centered"><ds-loading _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-loading _nghost-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="spinner spinner-border ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3410226373="" class="sr-only">Cargando...</span></div><!----></ds-themed-loading><!----></ds-loading></div></div></div><!----><img _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1027064000="" class="thumbnail-content img-fluid d-none ng-star-inserted" src="" alt="Miniatura"><!----><!----></div></ds-themed-thumbnail><!----></ds-thumbnail></a><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="col-9"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="d-flex"><ds-badges _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-badges _nghost-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted"><ds-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----></ds-themed-status-badge><!----></ds-status-badge><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363=""><ds-type-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="pe-1" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-type-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="sr-only">Item type:</span><span class="badge bg-info">Ítem</span><span class="sr-only">, </span></span><!----></ds-themed-type-badge><!----></ds-type-badge><ds-access-status-badge _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1603002363="" class="ng-star-inserted" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-access-status-badge class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-themed-access-status-badge><!----></ds-access-status-badge><!----></div></ds-themed-badges><!----></ds-badges><!----></div><ds-truncatable _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c1371919000="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1371919000=""><a _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="lead item-list-title dont-break-out ng-star-inserted" href="/items/a0eca249-57ed-4111-931e-a3581259d4fb" target="_self">Occurrence of cryptosporidium sp. in fresh produce from the metropolitan area of Costa Rica: an update</a><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="text-muted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-1 min-1"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"> (<!----><!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-date ng-star-inserted">2026</span><!---->) <!----><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-authors ng-star-inserted"><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Murillo Salas, Nelly</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Alvarado Ocampo, Johan</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Abrahams Sandí, Elizabeth</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Retana Moreira, Lissette</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="ng-star-inserted">; </span><!----><ds-metadata-link-view _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" class="d-inline-block ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3805467724="" data-test="textWithoutIcon" class="ng-star-inserted">Chaves Ulate, Carolina</span><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-metadata-link-view><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></span><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" class="item-list-abstract ng-star-inserted"><ds-truncatable-part _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c3141691363=""><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="clamp-default-3 min-3"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="content dont-break-out preserve-line-breaks removeFaded"><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3132354919="">Foodborne diseases represent a major global public health problem, causing significant morbidity and mortality, and substantial economic losses. Fruits and vegetables are considered among the main vehicles for transmission of infectious agents like bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites, including Cryptosporidium sp. This protozoan parasite comprises many species that infect a wide range of hosts, is environmentally and geographically ubiquitous and has become one of the leading causes of diarrheal disease; in immunocompromised hosts, the infection can result in a chronic, life-threatening disease. Considering the importance of fruit and vegetable consumption in the daily diet and the need to ensure their safety, the aim of the study was to evaluate the presence of Cryptosporidium sp. in strawberries, lettuce and cilantro marketed in the Metropolitan Area of Costa Rica and to assess the degree of faecal contamination in these foods. For this purpose, 96 samples were analysed using parasitological and molecular methods that included a nested PCR to amplify Cryptosporidium sp. gp60 gene. Moreover, the presence of total and thermotolerant coliforms and Escherichia coli was also determined by culture methods and counts, for further identification using the VITEK system. Direct examination of wet mount and Ziehl-Neelsen stains revealed five Cryptosporidium sp. positive samples by microscopy and 22 positive samples by PCR; the identified species was Cryptosporidium parvum. Cilantro samples presented the highest counts of total, and thermotolerant coliforms and E. coli was identified in14 samples among 82 samples subjected to bacteriological analyses. The detection of C. parvum in raw vegetables and fruits from different provinces in Costa Rica, particularly using molecular techniques, demonstrates the need to strengthen surveillance and control in the production and marketing of these foods, to improve risk assessment and its relevance to public health.</span></div><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" dsdragclick="" role="button" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-link expandButton p-0" aria-expanded="false"><i _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="fa-angle-down fas"></i><span _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c3141691363="" class="ms-1">Más...</span></button></div></ds-truncatable-part></div><!----></div></ds-truncatable><!----></div></div></ds-item-search-result-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></ds-item-list-element><!----></ds-listable-object-component-loader></li><!----></ul><button _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c1978743132="" role="link" tabindex="0" class="btn btn-primary search-button mt-4 float-start ng-tns-c1978743132-3"> Cargar más ... </button></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ds-recent-item-list><!----><!----></div><!----><ds-suggestions-popup _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c4059863515="" _nghost-dspace-angular-c2693165288="" class="ng-tns-c2693165288-2 ng-star-inserted"><!----></ds-suggestions-popup><!----></ds-themed-home-page><!----></ds-home-page><!----></div></main><ds-footer _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c2344767681="" class="ng-tns-c2344767681-0" data-used-theme="kerwa"><ds-themed-footer _nghost-dspace-angular-c639509871="" class="ng-star-inserted"><footer _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c639509871=""><!----><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c639509871="" class="bottom-footer p-1 d-flex flex-column flex-md-row justify-content-center align-items-center text-white"><div _ngcontent-dspace-angular-c639509871="" class="cont