a, Leonel","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"0fd4fa63-5a9b-4b20-aa5d-1efaa66956fa","language":null,"value":"Abrahams Sandí, Elizabeth","place":6,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"3514b34e-30ef-4313-b836-2796b80c7a9b","language":null,"value":"Retana Moreira, Lissette","place":7,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.accessioned":[{"uuid":"aafb65ba-d656-4d23-97db-9d3194f07df2","language":null,"value":"2026-10-28T22:18:49Z","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.issued":[{"uuid":"6205fefe-01b8-4813-bdbe-a0f6cd7d3178","language":null,"value":"2026","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.abstract":[{"uuid":"b9368af2-4dc5-4a98-a95a-3d0e3164cf3b","language":null,"value":"Free-living amoebae (FLA) of the Vahlkampfiidae family are widely distributed in nature, occupying aquatic and terrestrial habitats. The group includes thermophilic amphizoic organisms such as Naegleria fowleri. This study aims to describe natural recreational freshwaters in terms of the presence of thermotolerant vahlkampfiids, sediment microbial communities and climatic/land use features.  Water samples were collected from 24 locations from Costa Rica. DNA was extracted from FLA cultivated at 42 °C and molecular identification using family and N. fowleri species-specific primers for conventional PCR was performed. DNA extractions of sediment samples were also performed for a microbial metabarcoding characterization approach through 16S rRNA V3-V4 region and 18S rRNA V4 region gene amplicons sequencing. A geographic information system was used to locate each sampling site in its respective climatic subregion and to establish a land use coverage buffer around it. Results revealed 20 positive locations for vahlkampfiids; the sites predominantly featured forest cover and were in climatic subregions with significant rainfall patterns. All locations were negative for N. fowleri; however, identification by sequencing detected a predominance of Tetramitus spp., followed by Vahlkampfia sp. and Neovahlkampfia sp. Sediment metabarcoding showed mainly metazoans, microalgae and Proteobacteria in these benthic ecosystems. Even when N. fowleri was not found, our exploration showed that these aquatic environments of close human contact allow the presence of thermotolerant vahlkampfiids and might be surrounded by microbial communities of interest for future research regarding ecological interactions and public health risks.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.procedence":[{"uuid":"3b9310f2-d9da-4d17-b98f-ab47be604980","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Docencia::Salud::Facultad de Microbiología","place":0,"authority":"ucr:FMi","confidence":600},{"uuid":"a1a8bf79-7cfa-4590-9ffe-0f56c033b674","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Investigación::Unidades de Investigación::Ciencias de la Salud::Centro de Investigación en Enfermedades Tropicales (CIET)","place":1,"authority":"ucr:UI-S-2","confidence":600},{"uuid":"9afa6456-40c5-4b89-b22c-6b092d27fced","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Investigación::Unidades de Investigación::Ciencias Básicas::Centro en Investigación en Contaminación Ambiental (CICA)","place":2,"authority":"ucr:UI-CB-13","confidence":600}],"dc.description.sponsorship":[{"uuid":"94b6c5d1-289f-45ca-b32f-c8313ee43581","language":null,"value":"Centro de Investigación en Enfermedades Tropicales/[803-C3513]/CIET/Costa Rica","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.citation":[{"uuid":"acb5c0a1-c942-40c0-a567-25750b6687ec","language":null,"value":"www.frontiersin.org/journals/microbiology","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.doi":[{"uuid":"22932a51-7eaf-43e9-b6c1-109a0ef7d23c","language":null,"value":"803-C3513","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.uri":[{"uuid":"5e22ed15-8937-44db-bf83-637446aeed10","language":null,"value":"https://hdl.handle.net/10669/105344","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.language.iso":[{"uuid":"308c37a8-35cc-442e-95cc-d547bb8d445c","language":null,"value":"eng","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.rights":[{"uuid":"68062704-8718-478c-ad18-789c189deb5c","language":null,"value":"acceso abierto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.source":[{"uuid":"7f839561-3d08-43de-be3d-26169be161a9","language":null,"value":"Frontiers in Microbiology","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject":[{"uuid":"6c9d47bd-a4f5-461e-b403-17e82d36c9e1","language":null,"value":"Vahlkampfiidae","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"259ceed6-69db-47d3-9da8-173df09a90d8","language":null,"value":"Naegleria","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"860c47d8-3f73-424d-a0ea-550d3f0ea1f8","language":null,"value":"climate","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"84dced23-856c-4b24-83b8-98babfa54e08","language":null,"value":"land use","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"4d27c7ec-3488-4cba-9137-cd945664b41b","language":null,"value":"metabarcoding.","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"a9b70498-e7a0-4c0f-9d2a-b247555faf89","language":null,"value":"Exploring the neighborhood of thermotolerant free-living amoebae in Costa Rican natural water reservoirs as a preliminary One Health approach in the field","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.type":[{"uuid":"fc15191a-69bf-447c-8193-2d9cecae571d","language":null,"value":"artículo preliminar","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292828123,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":[],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":[]},"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48":{"data":{"sizeBytes":3065,"checkSum":{"checkSumAlgorithm":"MD5","value":"cf54608c0ae277d4e44e1457ba036dbb"},"bundleName":"THUMBNAIL","_links":{"content":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48/content"},"bundle":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48/bundle"},"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48/accessStatus"},"format":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48/format"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48/thumbnail"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48"}},"_name":"Dolarización financiera y rentabilidad bancaria en Costa Rica.pdf.jpg","id":"24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48","uuid":"24aefd14-3e50-4343-b1b7-d497bebc0f48","type":"bitstream","metadata":{"dc.description":[{"uuid":"c4ac07b0-20d1-4bbb-b2c4-cf04298e1503","language":null,"value":"Generated Thumbnail","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.source":[{"uuid":"87967d69-cd6c-450f-8c8a-7ce42725bf36","language":null,"value":"Written by FormatFilter org.dspace.app.mediafilter.PDFBoxThumbnail on 2026-10-29T03:01:05Z (GMT).","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"595600f8-b9aa-4765-963a-0f6628621bbd","language":null,"value":"Dolarización financiera y rentabilidad bancaria en Costa Rica.pdf.jpg","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292828124,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":["https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/thumbnail"]},"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9":{"data":{"handle":"10669/105343","lastModified":"2026-10-29T03:01:05.853Z","isArchived":true,"isDiscoverable":true,"isWithdrawn":false,"entityType":null,"_links":{"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/accessStatus"},"bundles":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/bundles"},"identifiers":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/identifiers"},"mappedCollections":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/mappedCollections"},"owningCollection":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/owningCollection"},"relationships":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/relationships"},"version":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/version"},"templateItemOf":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/templateItemOf"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/thumbnail"},"submitter":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9/submitter"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9"}},"_name":"Dolarización financiera y rentabilidad bancaria en Costa Rica: un análisis empírico del impacto de la especialización en productos en dólares con enfoque econométrico y regulatorio","id":"28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9","uuid":"28aa27f5-bd6e-4d30-bd7e-f950e531e9a9","type":"item","metadata":{"dc.contributor.advisor":[{"uuid":"4b090b4b-3510-4da9-8bb5-f5a073182910","language":null,"value":"Cantillo Simón, Miguel","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.creator":[{"uuid":"8bfac8db-8954-4f8a-82be-ceb0886693d5","language":null,"value":"Abarca Chinchilla, Óscar Eduardo","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"6a33f66d-5076-40d2-8029-bbfa3debaa1d","language":null,"value":"Astorga Hernández, Édgar Eduardo","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"b31dc26b-5da8-4e7f-9136-7004ba12e407","language":null,"value":"Castillo Castro, César Augusto","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.accessioned":[{"uuid":"f0664e78-e05c-4822-802e-41f7b3d8ed3f","language":null,"value":"2026-10-28T21:21:20Z","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.issued":[{"uuid":"cba0bb1e-ee3d-4417-b584-52fa00b01b49","language":null,"value":"2026","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.abstract":[{"uuid":"29bbd5eb-1099-494d-b86f-ec6def263635","language":null,"value":"Esta investigación analiza la relación entre el grado de especialización en productos financieros denominados en dólares y la rentabilidad de los bancos comerciales costarricenses entre enero del 2008 y diciembre del 2025. Combina un análisis descriptivo, la estimación de un panel dinámico de coeficientes heterogéneos con dependencia transversal mediante el enfoque Common Correlated Effects Mean Group (CCEMG) de Chudik y Pesaran (2015) —complementada con ejercicios de robustez de efectos fijos dinámicos y errores estándar de Driscoll y Kraay (1998)— y una discusión regulatoria comparada. Como variable dependiente se utiliza un ROE ajustado que aísla el efecto contable de la revaluación cambiaria. La evidencia descriptiva muestra una diferenciación estructural persistente entre bancos públicos y privados, con posiciones cambiarias y carteras en dólares mayores en estos últimos. Los resultados econométricos indican que la dolarización de la cartera no es un determinante significativo del ROE a nivel sistémico; la rentabilidad se explica consistentemente por la persistencia del ROE, la capitalización y la eficiencia operativa, destacando la diversificación de ingresos como el determinante de mayor impacto positivo. Además, un aumento de 1 p.p. en la tasa de depreciación mensual del colón reduce el ROE operativo en 0.18 p.p., aun tras aislar la revaluación contable. Así, el crédito en dólares opera más como instrumento de captación y fidelización de clientes que como fuente de rédito: la banca privada asume riesgos cambiarios y crediticios significativos sin una contraprestación clara en el retorno ajustado por riesgo. A la luz de la experiencia de Turquía, Uruguay y Ecuador, ello refuerza la necesidad de fortalecer el marco prudencial costarricense, en particular la prueba de tensión BUST aplicada por la SUGEF.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"e3907a9e-994b-4869-86c3-c2d86594d05e","language":null,"value":"This research analyzes the relationship between the degree of specialization in U.S. dollardenominated financial products and the profitability of Costa Rican commercial banks from January 2008 to December 2025. It combines a descriptive analysis, the estimation of a dynamic heterogeneous-coefficient panel with cross-sectional dependence using the Common Correlated Effects Mean Group (CCEMG) approach of Chudik and Pesaran (2015) —complemented by robustness exercises with dynamic fixed effects and Driscoll and Kraay (1998) standard errors— and a comparative regulatory discussion. The dependent variable is an adjusted ROE that isolates the accounting effect of exchange rate revaluation. The descriptive evidence shows a persistent structural differentiation between public and private banks, with larger foreign exchange positions and dollar portfolios in the latter. The econometric results indicate that loan portfolio dollarization is not a significant determinant of ROE at the systemic level; profitability is consistently explained by ROE persistence, capitalization, and operating efficiency, with income diversification standing out as the determinant with the largest positive impact. Moreover, a 1 p.p. increase in the monthly depreciation rate of the colón lowers operating ROE by 0.18 p.p., even after isolating the accounting revaluation. Dollar lending thus operates more as an instrument for customer acquisition and retention than as a source of return: private banks assume significant foreign exchange and credit risks without a clear counterpart in risk-adjusted returns. In light of the experience of Turkey, Uruguay, and Ecuador, this reinforces the need to strengthen the Costa Rican prudential framework, particularly the BUST stress test applied by SUGEF.","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.procedence":[{"uuid":"89adbb90-3bcc-417b-ae85-45fa4946b7ea","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Docencia::Ciencias Sociales::Facultad de Ciencias Económicas::Escuela de Economía","place":0,"authority":"ucr:FCE3","confidence":600},{"uuid":"66b23e42-19fd-4531-842a-9cbddbeab2f1","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Investigación::Sistema de Estudios de Posgrado::Ciencias Sociales::Maestría Profesional en Finanzas y Riesgo","place":1,"authority":"ucr:SEP-CS-98","confidence":600}],"dc.identifier.uri":[{"uuid":"f2adfc6a-879a-43ed-b9f5-36a0f0105877","language":null,"value":"https://hdl.handle.net/10669/105343","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.language.iso":[{"uuid":"2eee4ab4-2a04-4e20-9563-667f2583c7db","language":null,"value":"spa","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.rights":[{"uuid":"d88ae1d0-c970-4468-9ee4-31b6a4266ae6","language":null,"value":"acceso abierto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.source":[{"uuid":"0368ad85-216a-43a7-8587-838cf8bb4f61","language":null,"value":"San José, Costa Rica: Universidad de Costa Rica.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject":[{"uuid":"57b83cb6-224b-46ad-8800-eb2282fabe12","language":null,"value":"Dolarización financiera","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"a07aaacd-cf97-4b94-ac9a-5ed2a86c96e9","language":null,"value":"Rentabilidad bancaria","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"5e591669-2399-4f9e-b005-de2b672af47d","language":null,"value":"Riesgo cambiario","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"f08219f1-4e52-4282-8d79-aa9a6f89f47e","language":null,"value":"Descalce cambiario","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"9ce26d9b-0621-4a86-b5bd-e65bea36b32a","language":null,"value":"Panel dinámico heterogéneo","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"d288e721-ec56-4a5b-b8f5-15e8a9840b06","language":null,"value":"Regulación prudencial","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"3abaed0b-c04a-4e79-8bea-d6f436a0b57e","language":null,"value":"Costa Rica","place":6,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"1b0de08a-5abe-4113-9601-2712242adce1","language":null,"value":"Financial dollarization","place":7,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"2e890da9-c00c-4668-b6a5-01a2ea4fff08","language":null,"value":"Bank profitability","place":8,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"658c30c8-c517-4353-b25d-b5774b9c08d9","language":null,"value":"Foreign exchange risk","place":9,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"b50ff91c-6982-45d9-b32f-637671767316","language":null,"value":"Currency mismatch","place":10,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"ddf9a926-78f7-4de3-8d35-56872ddca87d","language":null,"value":"Heterogeneous dynamic panel","place":11,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"552f254f-3a09-425b-8eb2-4d0611a8726a","language":null,"value":"Common Correlated Effects Mean Group (CCEMG)","place":12,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"6c86fd59-cce9-4a50-9410-8a5f4ef299c1","language":null,"value":"Prudential regulation","place":13,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"a920aa48-1c55-41a9-a8b7-fd6cf0df99ef","language":null,"value":"Dolarización financiera y rentabilidad bancaria en Costa Rica: un análisis empírico del impacto de la especialización en productos en dólares con enfoque econométrico y regulatorio","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.type":[{"uuid":"6f140832-5728-4436-b843-2de37b5bf6d6","language":null,"value":"tesis de maestría","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292828125,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":[],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":[]},"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009":{"data":{"sizeBytes":2671,"checkSum":{"checkSumAlgorithm":"MD5","value":"ce14d94f469afb07776132c9d21e7318"},"bundleName":"THUMBNAIL","_links":{"content":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009/content"},"bundle":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009/bundle"},"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009/accessStatus"},"format":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009/format"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009/thumbnail"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009"}},"_name":"Tesis Luis Enrique Mata Quintero.pdf.jpg","id":"d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009","uuid":"d76c423e-7571-4453-9b6b-d095d4abd009","type":"bitstream","metadata":{"dc.description":[{"uuid":"66bdcfdf-9bd2-4415-93d6-5a95f1ee64d0","language":null,"value":"Generated Thumbnail","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.source":[{"uuid":"99759899-5e08-4594-a3d5-deab89f32ea2","language":null,"value":"Written by FormatFilter org.dspace.app.mediafilter.PDFBoxThumbnail on 2026-10-29T03:01:00Z (GMT).","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"ce41072a-5842-4a07-ba3f-e4413deb9ab2","language":null,"value":"Tesis Luis Enrique Mata Quintero.pdf.jpg","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292828126,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":["https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/thumbnail"]},"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df":{"data":{"handle":"10669/105342","lastModified":"2026-10-29T03:01:00.538Z","isArchived":true,"isDiscoverable":true,"isWithdrawn":false,"entityType":null,"_links":{"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/accessStatus"},"bundles":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/bundles"},"identifiers":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/identifiers"},"mappedCollections":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/mappedCollections"},"owningCollection":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/owningCollection"},"relationships":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/relationships"},"version":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/version"},"templateItemOf":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/templateItemOf"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/thumbnail"},"submitter":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df/submitter"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/items/251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df"}},"_name":"La transgresión del límite (πεῖρας) como problema fundamental del filosofar en el poema de Parménides","id":"251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df","uuid":"251bc755-84ba-4d84-ad41-6e8139d0c3df","type":"item","metadata":{"dc.contributor.advisor":[{"uuid":"556a42d2-b332-4ec1-9947-c0542612a6ac","language":null,"value":"Fallas López, Luis Alberto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.creator":[{"uuid":"24a9cb3c-75bb-4c26-811c-b80f699fddba","language":null,"value":"Mata Quintero, Luis Enrique","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.accessioned":[{"uuid":"886a856e-4255-4d9c-9948-ef9f5a4a6746","language":null,"value":"2026-10-28T21:17:14Z","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.issued":[{"uuid":"d56c2398-870f-4bc8-950b-37c63e6e3011","language":null,"value":"2026","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.abstract":[{"uuid":"9e434be1-d601-4b74-86bd-f8dec37e033a","language":null,"value":"Esta investigación aborda el problema de la transgresión del límite (πεῖρας) como eje interpretativo de la filosofía de Parménides, proponiendo una lectura que integra los aspectos poéticos, religiosos y filosóficos del Poema. Frente a la tendencia de la tradición interpretativa a centrarse exclusivamente en la noción de límite, este estudio sostiene que el pensamiento parmenídeo no solo lo establece, sino que también piensa la posibilidad de su exceso, es decir, la inclinación del filosofar mismo a transgredir dichos límites. \n\nEl trabajo parte de la hipótesis de que el filosofar en Parménides implica, de manera constitutiva, una condición transgresora del pensar, aunque la idea de transgresión no debe entenderse de manera unívoca, pues si bien el pensar tiende al exceso, no todo exceso es ilegítimo. La investigación distingue entre exceso —como impulso hacia lo desconocido y apertura del pensar— y transgresión —como quiebre ilegítimo de los límites de lo posible— , y muestra que la tensión entre ambos constituye el núcleo de la experiencia filosófica. \n\nPara fundamentar esta tesis, se examina el contexto pre-parmenídeo del problema, desde la épica de Homero y Hesíodo hasta los filósofos milesios, pitagóricos, Jenófanes y Heráclito, donde el límite se concibe como la distancia entre lo humano y lo divino. A partir de este trasfondo, en el segundo capítulo se ofrece una relectura del Proemio como una metáfora del ingreso a la filosofía, en la que el κοῦρος simboliza el tránsito del mortal hacia un ámbito reservado a los dioses. El viaje descrito por el Poema se interpreta como una experiencia limítrofe en la que el pensamiento, movido por el exceso, arriesga incurrir en la transgresión. En el tercer capítulo, el estudio se centra en la revelación de la Diosa, mostrando que el conocimiento verdadero posee un carácter excesivo para los mortales: el νοεῖν que capta el ἐόν trasciende la condición humana y exige una transformación del pensamiento. A través del análisis de los fragmentos B 1, 2, 3, 6 y 7, se concluye que Parménides no se limita a fijar los límites del pensar, sino que invita a explorarlos, asumiendo el riesgo inherente de la transgresión. \n\nDe este modo, la tesis demuestra que la filosofía parmenídea surge de una tensión fundamental entre el límite y su transgresión, entre la necesidad de contener el pensar y la inclinación inevitable a desbordarlo. Pensar el límite implica, en Parménides, rozar lo inalcanzable, y es precisamente en ese gesto donde el filosofar se revela como una forma de exceso constitutivo del pensamiento mismo.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"70065ae4-261a-4cad-9db6-dcf041a12f55","language":null,"value":"This research addresses the problem of the transgression of the limit (πεῖρας) as the central interpretive focus of Parmenides’ philosophy, proposing a reading that integrates the poetic, religious, and philosophical dimensions of the Poem. In contrast to the interpretative tradition’s tendency to focus exclusively on the notion of the limit, this study argues that Parmenidean thought not only establishes it, but also reflects on the possibility of its excess— that is, on philosophy’s own inclination to transgress such boundaries. \n\nThe work begins from the hypothesis that philosophizing in Parmenides inherently entails a transgressive condition of thought, although the idea of transgression should not be understood univocally: while thought tends toward excess, not every excess is illegitimate. The research distinguishes between excess—as an impulse toward the unknown and an opening of thought—and transgression—as the illegitimate crossing of the limits of what is possible—and shows that the tension between the two constitutes the core of the philosophical experience. \n\nTo substantiate this thesis, the pre-Parmenidean context of the problem is examined, from the epic poetry of Homer and Hesiod to the Milesian philosophers, Pythagoreans, Xenophanes, and Heraclitus, where the limit is conceived as the distance between the human and the divine. Against this background, the second chapter offers a reinterpretation of the Proem as a metaphor for the initiation into philosophy, in which the κοῦρος symbolizes the mortal’s passage into a realm reserved for the gods. The journey described in the Poem is interpreted as a liminal experience in which thought, driven by excess, risks falling into transgression. The third chapter focuses on the revelation of the Goddess, showing that true knowledge possesses an excessive character for mortals: the νοεῖν that grasps the ἐόν transcends the human condition and demands a transformation of thought. Through an analysis of fragments B 1, 2, 3, 6, and 7, the study concludes that Parmenides does not merely establish the limits of thought but invites us to explore them, embracing the inherent risk of transgression. \n\nThus, the thesis demonstrates that Parmenidean philosophy arises from a fundamental tension between the limit and its transgression, between the need to contain thought and its inevitable inclination to overflow. To think about the limit, in Parmenides, is to touch the unreachable, and it is precisely in this gesture that philosophy reveals itself as a constitutive excess of thought itself.","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.procedence":[{"uuid":"290c1f26-ccaf-43dd-bec6-e450101bf950","language":null,"value":"Vicerrectoría de Investigación::Sistema de Estudios de Posgrado::Artes y Letras::Maestría Académica en Filosofía","place":0,"authority":"ucr:SEP-AL-9","confidence":600}],"dc.identifier.uri":[{"uuid":"ece6a329-5f33-4d8f-9452-8b34df44cd74","language":null,"value":"https://hdl.handle.net/10669/105342","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.language.iso":[{"uuid":"05c726f9-66f6-4858-8c2b-7f4fe6cecb8b","language":null,"value":"spa","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.rights":[{"uuid":"44120585-2329-42a5-9d3e-271b850f46fa","language":null,"value":"acceso abierto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.source":[{"uuid":"476f60b7-0e7c-4825-87ed-6c640b318aba","language":null,"value":"San José, Costa Rica: Universidad de Costa Rica.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject":[{"uuid":"bde7fbea-e210-48f0-9a93-9441f88cd021","language":null,"value":"Filosofía","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"299fabdd-bd4c-4812-bd8b-e52bc0b1d33b","language":null,"value":"Parménides","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"3dc821de-1b6d-4a99-b962-e99dc60831d4","language":null,"value":"Transgresión del límite","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"6aa70a55-f359-48bf-aeb9-9b527f31d1ed","language":null,"value":"Exceso","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"985af967-68fe-4ec8-a191-5b0109477936","language":null,"value":"Conocimiento","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"9be45fc7-1481-4a8e-9975-57cb943e9930","language":null,"value":"Ontología","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"be70b9b8-0d1f-4f7d-9d30-7c06df6071c1","language":null,"value":"Philosophy","place":6,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"ba3eae2c-3fc3-4f1f-8a08-502d7f81032e","language":null,"value":"Transgression of the limit","place":7,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"01c2fcab-7b99-4ef1-9e29-133f3916c371","language":null,"value":"Excess","place":8,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"0dba59f5-14dc-4b0a-9c18-b68b431d7988","language":null,"value":"Knowledge","place":9,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"ec1df940-5e3c-4364-b26f-daa098965b79","language":null,"value":"Ontology","place":10,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"80faee38-db3f-4114-9b47-b250a8e80902","language":null,"value":"La transgresión del límite (πεῖρας) como problema fundamental del filosofar en el poema de Parménides","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.type":[{"uuid":"e7f9d16d-66ec-4031-b079-288854f7f957","language":null,"value":"tesis de maestría","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292828127,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/f9b9b344-8697-4028-a67f-101decbd6798"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":[],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":[]},"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/ea4f467e-6d67-4a0e-9888-1cd0496023a7":{"data":{"sizeBytes":3020,"checkSum":{"checkSumAlgorithm":"MD5","value":"9a7dc15b045bf2aa9888f917b65c180c"},"bundleName":"THUMBNAIL","_links":{"content":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/ea4f467e-6d67-4a0e-9888-1cd0496023a7/content"},"bundle":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/ea4f467e-6d67-4a0e-9888-1cd0496023a7/bundle"},"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/ea4f467e-6d67-4a0e-9888-1cd0496023a7/accessStatus"},"format":{"href":"https://repositorio.ucr.ac.cr/server/api/core/bitstreams/ea4f467e-6d67-4a0e-9888-1cd0496023a7/